# The magnetic keyboard's touchpad sits on the tablet's pogo-pin i2c bus, so
# libinput falls back to its bus-type heuristic and classifies it as an
# internal touchpad.  Internal touchpads are suspended whenever the tablet-mode
# switch is on (libinput, evdev-mt-touchpad.c: tp_pair_tablet_mode_switch).
#
# That used to be worked around by inverting the hall polarity in the device
# tree, which made the touchpad work but also stopped GNOME's automatic
# rotation: Mutter only manages the built-in panel orientation while the seat
# is in tablet mode (mutter, meta-seat-impl.c: update_touch_mode), so a hall
# reporting "not tablet" in laptop position disables rotation and hides the
# rotation lock.
#
# Tagging the touchpad external keeps libinput from suspending it while the
# tablet-mode hall keeps its upstream polarity, so both the touchpad and
# automatic rotation work.  The rule matches the input device name; the pogo
# keyboard enumerates as "Xiaomi Touch" (touchpad), "Xiaomi Mouse",
# "Xiaomi Keyboard" and "Xiaomi Consumer".
ACTION=="add|change", SUBSYSTEM=="input", ATTRS{name}=="Xiaomi Touch", ENV{ID_INPUT_TOUCHPAD_INTEGRATION}="external"
